tlife","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"Coffee & Tea, Food","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"u08-CrCg_f9sdGD5BtL-QA","review_id":"hDq-CKKKZNNVUpORODkHWw","date":"2021-08-24T02:35:23","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9440608620643616,"text_excerpt":"This is the coffee shop of my dreams. Easily my favorite place to get a drink, coffee, and hang out in New Orleans. The Irish museum attached is so cute and I was so excited to hear from the bartender that this place is family owned and run. He gave us some great tips and places to visit. I just loved the atmosphere. I felt so relaxed. The London fog was absolutely incredible and so was the Dublin fog cocktail. We happened to be there during a thunderstorm and the little seating area was like it was out of a storybook. Loved it!"},{"business_id":"u08-CrCg_f9sdGD5BtL-QA","review_id":"M2Ut5hH9WF09FcLI68i3HA","date":"2021-10-23T17:55:31","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9354656934738159,"text_excerpt":"After walking by hundreds of times on my way to what is now my second favorite iced coffee in the city, I finally gave St. Pat's a chance to impress... and impress it did! Super chill, spotlessly clean, comfortable courtyard and cozy inside bar space with family history galore. Small museum with even more Irish memorabilia. The super friendly family who runs the bar will gladly talk Irish history for as long as you'd like to do so. As awesome as the space and service is, Irish cocktails are the real reason you're here, and I assure you that they are amazing. I was in the mood for an iced Irish coffee. Handmade. Not too sweet, not too strong... absolutely perfect! Can't wait to come back f..."},{"business_id":"u08-CrCg_f9sdGD5BtL-QA","review_id":"8RN-j0XdFwobnLBsikSvqA","date":"2018-08-21T02:12:18","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9345675110816956,"text_excerpt":"\"There are no strangers here; Only friends you haven't yet met.\" - W. B. Yeats We were looking for a coffee place to chill, enjoy some quiet time on WiFi (NOLA gets pretty noisy :-) and we ended up getting a delicious local beer, chatting with Matthew, warmhearted and amazing owner of this place. We got to meet his sons and their girlfriends and we felt like part of his family :-) And yes, in the end, we got some coffee too. It took us a while to find this place, don't expect big signs or neon lights :-) My first impression was - this is a bar, not a coffee shop. But man, their coffee was the best we have had in NOLA. As I mentioned above, Matthew was very friendly and kind. We have learn..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"u08-CrCg_f9sdGD5BtL-QA","photo_id":"MFhrQGgqKuAhTbPkWci48Q","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/MFhrQGgqKuAhTbPkWci48Q.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9123365879058838},{"business_id":"u08-CrCg_f9sdGD5BtL-QA","photo_id":"bFYyHvqFBL6D8LSiwjJdcg","label":"outside","image_url":"/photos/bFYyHvqFBL6D8LSiwjJdcg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8801320791244507},{"business_id":"u08-CrCg_f9sdGD5BtL-QA","photo_id":"Q1dtZwgiGHumD9cmioy2bw","label":"drink","image_url":"/photos/Q1dtZwgiGHumD9cmioy2bw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8334962129592896}]},"notebook_case":null}
